When you look at the game it's look like one of the "classic" zombie survival games. But inside, game has too many options and details. You can craft almost everything in game, kill zombies, build a safehouse, bake breads, grow tomatoes and make a tomato juicy etc. but the game needs too much time for make a progress.
So;
Don't recommended. But if you're a 4-5 (or more) friends and looking for full detailed zombie survival game, this game is good choise for you.

MASTERPIECE. It's good as a game, it's better as a piece of art.
Graphics quality isn't bad as this game is 10 years old already;
Musics is just great;
It really has lore;
You can find reference of your favorite games, and what other games take references of;
Characters come to life.
I am a big fan of BioShock Infinite, and then I tried the first BS--simply stunning. I can't really tell which one is better, these two really both have great stories and interesting theories.
With Infinite and BaS DLCs, the whole franchise becomes a full circle.
There is always a city. It can be something like rapture in Bioshock, it can also be Columbia. It can be anything.
There is always a man.
I wasn't there when the game was released. Ten years ago, I was into other things than FPS. Now it's 2017 and after playing it, I'd say  it's worth every single dollar I spent.
YES, IT'S BEEN TEN YEARS AND PEOPLE STILL LOVE IT.
MORE IMPORTANTLY, THERE ARE SOLID REASONS TO LOVE THIS GAME.

